Package: anydoc
Title: Convert Documents to Markdown
Version: 0.1.0
Authors@R: c(
    person("Pedro", "Baltazar", email = "pedrobtz@gmail.com",
           role = c("aut", "cre", "cph")),
    person("Firecrawl", role = "cph",
           comment = "author of the 'anydoc' Rust crate")
  )
Description: Converts 'Microsoft Word', 'PowerPoint' and 'Excel' documents,
    'OpenDocument' files, Rich Text Format (RTF), Electronic Publication
    (EPUB), comma-separated values (CSV) and Portable Document Format (PDF)
    files to Markdown, in the 'GitHub' Flavored Markdown dialect. The
    conversion is performed by the 'anydoc'
    <https://github.com/firecrawl/anydoc> 'Rust' library, which is compiled
    and linked when the package is installed. The input format is detected
    from the file contents rather than from its extension, so a file carrying
    the wrong extension still converts correctly. Every format is rendered
    through a single Markdown serializer, so headings, tables and lists are
    represented consistently whichever parser handled the input.
